{"id":"CKG-BSG-VTE","version":"1.0.0","sourceId":"BSG-ESGE-2021","passageIds":["BSG-VTE-DEFERRAL","BSG-VTE-BRIDGE","BSG-VTE-TIME"],"anchor":"anticoagulationStart","summary":"The recent-VTE discussion favors postponing a high-risk endoscopic procedure beyond the initial three months of anticoagulation when postponement is safe. It distinguishes necessary low-risk procedures and discourages bridging in the DOAC context.","qualifications":["Narrative timing refers to starting anticoagulation; Table 3 also refers to time after VTE. Both dates are retained.","Necessary low-risk procedures have a distinct exception; this slice does not decide interruption or reconcile adjacent general DOAC guidance.","No stop, restart, aspirin-substitution or bridging prescription is generated."],"verification":"SEMANTIC_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},
{"id":"CKG-ACG-VTE","version":"1.0.0","sourceId":"ACG-CAG-2022","passageIds":["ACG-EXCLUSION","ACG-DEFER","ACG-VTE-TIME"],"anchor":"vteDate","summary":"The elective-endoscopy recommendations exclude patients at high thromboembolic risk, including acute lower-limb DVT or pulmonary embolism within three months; the guideline directs deferral of elective procedures for this group.","qualifications":["This is an applicability exclusion, not a standard DOAC interruption schedule.","It is not restricted to high-bleeding-risk procedures in this paragraph.","The exact three-month boundary and urgency still require clinical interpretation; a calculated date is not clearance."],"verification":"SEMANTIC_VERIFICATION_PENDING"}],
